course: dictionary
lesson: 132
title: Adverse, a word for bad or harmful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adverse means bad, harmful or not helpful. Use the words around it to check. «The trains were delayed by adverse weather.» Adverse weather is bad weather that causes problems, such as snow stopping trains.
explain: Adverse often goes with another word: adverse weather, adverse effect, adverse conditions or adverse reaction. Try the swap check by putting bad in place of adverse: «The trains were delayed by bad weather.» It still makes sense, so bad is a good meaning here.
explain: Adverse is a formal word. You will often find it in news, exams and medicine leaflets. «"Adverse event" is medical jargon for harm or injury caused by medical treatment.» Jargon is the special vocabulary of a group of experts, so when you meet it, look for the plain meaning in the clues.
fact: Adverse means bad, harmful or not helpful.
fact: An adverse effect or reaction is a harmful one, such as a medicine making someone ill.
fact: Adverse weather is bad weather that causes problems, such as delays to trains.
fact: Adverse is a formal word, and it often replaces bad in news, exams and health leaflets.
fact: «Adverse event» is medical jargon for harm or injury caused by medical treatment.
exercise: «The trains were delayed by adverse weather.» What does adverse mean here? | Sunny and warm | Very loud | Quick and easy | *Bad and causing problems
exercise: «The medicine had an adverse reaction, so the nurse stopped it.» What is an adverse reaction? | *A harmful side effect | A type of bandage | A happy result | A kind word from a doctor
exercise: Which word is a good swap for adverse in «adverse conditions»? | *bad | quiet | happy | cheap
test: «The hikers turned back because of adverse conditions on the mountain.» What does adverse mean here? | Quiet | Bright | *Harmful or bad | Helpful
test: Doctors call a harmful mistake from treatment an adverse event. Why do you think they use this word? | It means a happy party | It is only a word for the weather | It means a fast car | *It is formal medical jargon for harm caused by treatment
exam: Which sentence uses adverse correctly? | My adverse bike is bright red. | We ate an adverse lunch of soup. | *The storm brought adverse weather that closed the roads. | The adverse sunshine made the park happy.
